# Trinity responsive token discipline

Shared fluid scale lives in `src/styles/responsive-tokens.css` (imported from `globals.css`).

When adding or restyling UI (Access, logins, dealer portal, staff TRI, depot):

1. Prefer `--tri-font-*`, `--tri-space-*`, `--tri-page-gutter`, `--tri-content-max`, and hero via `--dp-hero-height` / `--tri-hero-height-capped`.
2. Do **not** introduce new hard-coded major type sizes or page padding that bypass the scale (one-off `clamp()` for a page title is OK only as a `var(--tri-font-*, …)` fallback).
3. No whole-page `transform: scale()`.
4. Keep content-driven media queries; short laptops already tighten via `@media (min-width: 1024px) and (max-height: 800px)` on the tokens.
5. Wide data tables: horizontal scroll for now — dedicated mobile card/sheet UIs wait for mockups.
6. Preserve approved desktop compositions; scale and reflow only.
